{{Illusionnotes
| name = Impetus
| desc = Neither functional nor is [[toggled]] {{Symbol|Toggle|On}}.
}}
{{Stealnotes
| name = Impetus
| desc = Cannot acquire active {{M|attack modifiers}}.
| structure = hidden
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Impetus
| desc = Utilizes the caster's current {{M|attack range}} while {{M|Autocast}} is active, manual cast utilizes the ability's current {{M|cast range}}.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Attack Modifier}}
** Impetus is an active attack modifier, and has the following properties:
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|[[Cast Range|CastRange]] {{=}} Hero[[Attack Range|AtkRange]]}}
*** Affected by {{M|attack range}} sources of the same range-type as the caster.
** Both {{M|Autocast}} and an active cast uses Enchantress's current {{M|attack range}}.
*** Has Autocast off by default.
** {{Symbol|Attack Damage|Instant}}
*** This ability component can be applied by other [[instant attack]] sources.

* {{Symbol|Projectile|Impact}}
** The distance damage factor is calculated upon a successful {{M|projectile}} impact as follows:
**# The {{M|pure}} {{M|spell damage}}.
**#* The {{M|illusion}} damage factor is applied in a single damage instance in the {{M|combat log}}.
**# Enchantress' attack instance.

* Does not affect the following units:
** {{M|Allied units|x}}.
** {{M|Buildings}}
** {{M|Couriers}}
** {{M|Ward-type units}}.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Impetus icon0}}
| desc = Places an enchantment on each attack while activated, causing it to deal additional damage based on how far away the target is.  The farther the target, the greater the damage dealt. Deals double damage to illusions.
}}
* Deals a max {{calc|{{#var:Impetus value1}}*v1|v1={{#var:Impetus value2}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus t4r}} {{ValueColor||{{calc|{{#var:Impetus value1}}*v1|v1={{#var:Impetus value2 tal}}}}|25tal}}) {{M|pure}} {{M|spell damage}} at max distance.

{{Breaknotes
| name = Enchant
| desc = [[Break]] sources do not affect the {{M|talent}} granted {{M|auras}}.
}}
{{Stealnotes
| name = Enchant
| desc = The Enchanted unit is killed upon duration expiring, and not upon losing the ability.<br><br>Multiple casts of Enchant from opposing {{M|factions}} do not refresh its duration. The duration is only refreshed when cast on already Enchanted unit.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Enchant
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus agh}} [[Toggling]] {{M|autocast}} off {{M|swaps-out}} this ability with {{A|Enchantress|Little Friends}}.<br><br>Both abilities have independent {{M|cooldowns}}.
}}

{{Breaknotes
| name = Untouchable
| desc = [[Break]] sources disable the {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|enchantress_untouchable_slow}} functionality.<br><br>However, it does not prevent the debuff application.
}}

 * Applies a generic {{M|outgoing damage}} amplification on all {{M|neutral creeps}} and her {{M|Summons|text=player-controlled units}}.
** Stacks additively with other outgoing damage manipulation sources.
** Does not affect {{M|HP Removal}} sources.
** Does not affect the following units:
*** Enchantress' {{M|illusions}}.
*** {{M|Roshan}}
*** The {{M|Tormentor}}.

* {{cf|expr}}
** {{M|Outgoing damage}}: {{Code|{{#var:Rabble-Rouser basic1}} × SelfLVL}}

